a":"cyrillus_von_jerusalem","s":13,"p":[9,9],"r":[33,6],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Chron. xxxiii. 6."},{"id":"59e6bfe2b114","v":"npnf.kyrill_jer.catecheses","w":"kyrill_jer.catecheses","a":"cyrillus_von_jerusalem","s":17,"p":[31,31],"r":[15,1],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Chron. xv. 1."},{"id":"782ae0a24aa2","v":"npnf.theodoret.historia_ecclesiastica","w":"theodoret.historia_ecclesiastica","a":"theodoret_von_cyrus","s":3,"p":[62,62],"r":[24,8],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"The form in the text ( glwssokomon ) is rejected by Attic purists, but is used twice by St. John, as well as in the Septuagint. In II. Chron. xxiv. 8 (cf. II. Kings xii. 9) it means a chest. In St. John's Gospel xii. 6 and xiii. 29 it is \"the bag,\" properly (xi. 3) \"box,\" which Judas carried. In the Palatine anthology Nicanor the coffin maker makes these \"glossokoma\" or coffins. Derivatively the word means \"tongue-cases,\" i.e. cases to keep the tongues or reeds of musical instruments. An instance of similar transfer of meaning is our word \"coffin;\" derivatively a wicker basket; - at one time any case or cover, and in Shakespeare (Titus Andronicus Act V. 2, 189) pie crust. Perhaps \"casket,\" which now still holds many things, may one day only hold a corpse."},{"id":"d696837894ed","v":"npnf.cassian.de_institutis","w":"cassian.de_institutis","a":"johannes_cassian","s":3,"p":[32,32],"r":[7,9],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Collecta . This word, from which our word \"Collect\" is possibly derived is used for an assembly for worship in the Vulgate in Lev. xxiii. 36; Deut. xvi. 8; 2 Chron. vii. 9; Neh. viii. 18: and compare the phrase, \"Ad Collectam,\" in the Sacramentary of Gregory for the Feast of the Purification."},{"id":"b87da5002120","v":"npnf.cassian.de_institutis","w":"cassian.de_institutis","a":"johannes_cassian","s":11,"p":[29,29],"r":[32,24,32,26],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Chron. xxxii. 24-26."},{"id":"96530bb44857","v":"npnf.cassian.de_institutis","w":"cassian.de_institutis","a":"johannes_cassian","s":11,"p":[32,32],"r":[26,15],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Chron. xxvi. 15, 16."},{"id":"8b3643debfe1","v":"npnf.cassian.de_institutis","w":"cassian.de_institutis","a":"johannes_cassian","s":12,"p":[62,62],"r":[24,17],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Chr. xxiv. 17, 18; 23-25."},{"id":"c86b57bb8750","v":"npnf.cassian.conlationes","w":"cassian.conlationes","a":"johannes_cassian","s":1,"p":[58,58],"r":[3,5],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Obrizum . The word occurs in the Vulgate five times for \"pure gold.\" See 2 Chr. iii. 5; Job xxviii. 15; xxxi. 24; Isa. xiii. 12; Dan. x. 5; and is akin to the Greek o!brnzon . Cf. Pliny Nat. Hist. xxxiii. c. 3. and Jerome De Nom. Hebr. s. v. Ophaz."},{"id":"da69ac26a6a2","v":"npnf.cassian.conlationes","w":"cassian.conlationes","a":"johannes_cassian","s":7,"p":[39,39],"r":[6,30],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Chron. vi. 30."},{"id":"c070793701da","v":"csel.augustinus.de_peccatorum_meritis","w":"augustinus.de_peccatorum_meritis","a":"augustinus_von_hippo","s":3,"p":[3,3],"r":[19,7],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"medium","cited":"Sap. 4,11; IIPar. 19,7; Rom.9,14; Hier. 1, 5; Rom. 11, 33; Rom. 9, 11","note":"Stellenangabe im Apparat der Ausgabe (Seite; Absatz ungefähr)"}]}
